     The rest of the endgame doesn't cease to exist when you enter
the Astral Plane level; you just have no way (except in wizard mode)
to get back to the earlier planes.  But even if it did cease to exist,
that wouldn't stop the Wizard since he isn't saved with old levels.
He's kept with the list of monsters who are migrating (between levels,
waiting for you to activate their destination) and can be pulled off
of that to be brought to your level.  But this won't happen when your
level is the Astral Plane level because the randomly occurring "summon
Rodney our of thin air" effect is disallowed there.

     The most likely way for the Wizard to actually arrive on the
final level would be for him to be alive nearby when you go through
the portal.  He's one of the types of monsters who will tag along
when you use stairs or level teleport; they follow for portals too.
And he's not prevented from using his "double trouble" spell on the
Astral Plane, so you could have two of him.  But once he--or they, if
he has doubled--has been killed he couldn't come back again.


